Prime-power zero-branch cover cores -- codex S546b
==============================================================================
A q-zero branch is the set of speeds divisible by q=p^d.
If it is empty, unit times u/q are THM-369 sieve witnesses.
If it is covered, the local branch intervals are tested for a
nonpeeling endpoint-protection core.

