SYNTHESIS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Audited local branch cores: 86, nonempty=0
Audited full cover cores: 9, nonempty=0
Prime-power zero branches do exactly one thing locally: they kill
the unit sieve witnesses u/q.  Their local danger intervals are
nested around those unit points, so endpoint-core peeling deletes them.
Thus the branch does not store a counterexample core at q itself;
it exports endpoint debt to descendant wall/event layers.
For n=18 this matches the p-adic story: n*=9 makes zero-flow
branches abundant, but the audited cover cores remain empty.
